      <main class="article">
        <p class="intro">This fact sheet summarises the Claude Opus 4.6 model released by Anthropic: its position in the Claude family, key capabilities, intended use-cases, and how it compares with previous Claude releases and competing models.</p>

        <section class="section" aria-labelledby="at-a-glance">
          <h2 id="at-a-glance">At a Glance</h2>
          <table class="fact-table">
            <tr><th>Model</th><td>Claude Opus 4.6</td></tr>
            <tr><th>Developer</th><td>Anthropic</td></tr>
            <tr><th>Family</th><td>Claude 4.x (Opus tier — highest capability)</td></tr>
            <tr><th>Primary Focus</th><td>Advanced reasoning, code generation, multi-turn instruction following</td></tr>
            <tr><th>Context Window</th><td>Up to 200 000 tokens (input + output)</td></tr>
            <tr><th>Modalities</th><td>Text &amp; image input; text output</td></tr>
            <tr><th>API Access</th><td>Anthropic API, Amazon Bedrock, Google Cloud Vertex AI</td></tr>
            <tr><th>Release Window</th><td>Q4 2025 – Q1 2026 (iterative updates)</td></tr>
          </table>
        </section>

        <section class="section" aria-labelledby="capabilities">
          <h2 id="capabilities">Key Capabilities</h2>
          <ul class="clean">
            <li><strong>Extended reasoning:</strong> solves complex, multi-step problems in mathematics, science, law and software engineering with improved chain-of-thought accuracy.</li>
            <li><strong>Code mastery:</strong> generates, reviews and debugs code across 20+ languages; excels at large-codebase refactors and test generation.</li>
            <li><strong>Instruction fidelity:</strong> tighter alignment with developer prompts reduces hallucination and off-topic drift, especially in structured-output and tool-use scenarios.</li>
            <li><strong>Long-context coherence:</strong> maintains factual consistency and state tracking across 200k-token conversations and document analysis tasks.</li>
            <li><strong>Vision understanding:</strong> interprets charts, diagrams, screenshots and handwritten notes with improved spatial reasoning.</li>
            <li><strong>Safety &amp; alignment:</strong> constitutional AI training with enhanced refusal calibration — fewer false refusals on benign queries while maintaining robust guardrails.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="section" aria-labelledby="use-cases">
          <h2 id="use-cases">Intended Use-Cases</h2>
          <div class="compare" role="list">
            <article class="card" role="listitem" aria-label="Developer workflows">
              <h3>🛠️ Developer Workflows</h3>
              <p>Code generation, debugging, PR review, automated testing, documentation and architecture planning across full-stack projects.</p>
            </article>

            <article class="card" role="listitem" aria-label="Research and analysis">
              <h3>🔬 Research &amp; Analysis</h3>
              <p>Literature synthesis, data interpretation, hypothesis generation and long-document summarisation for academic and enterprise research teams.</p>
            </article>

            <article class="card" role="listitem" aria-label="Enterprise integration">
              <h3>🏢 Enterprise Integration</h3>
              <p>Customer support automation, internal knowledge retrieval, compliance review and workflow orchestration via tool-use and function calling.</p>
            </article>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="section" aria-labelledby="evolution">
          <h2 id="evolution">Evolution from Previous Claude Models</h2>
          <div class="compare" role="list">
            <article class="card" role="listitem" aria-label="Claude 3.5 Sonnet">
              <h3>Claude 3.5 Sonnet</h3>
              <p>Balanced speed and quality for everyday tasks. Opus 4.6 extends reasoning depth and context length significantly while retaining low-latency options via the Sonnet and Haiku tiers.</p>
            </article>

            <article class="card" role="listitem" aria-label="Claude Code 4.5 Opus">
              <h3>Claude Code 4.5 Opus</h3>
              <p>Code-specialised predecessor. Opus 4.6 inherits code strengths and adds broader general-knowledge improvements, vision input and a larger context window.</p>
            </article>

            <article class="card" role="listitem" aria-label="Claude Code 4.6 Opus">
              <h3>Claude Code 4.6 Opus</h3>
              <p>Current flagship. Combines the best of prior Opus and Sonnet advances: superior reasoning, expanded context, vision, and improved safety calibration in a single model.</p>
            </article>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="section" aria-labelledby="benchmarks">
          <h2 id="benchmarks">Selected Benchmarks (Indicative)</h2>
          <table class="fact-table">
            <tr><th>Benchmark</th><th>Opus 4.6</th><th>Prior Best (Claude)</th></tr>
            <tr><td>MMLU (5-shot)</td><td>~92%</td><td>~88% (3.5 Opus)</td></tr>
            <tr><td>HumanEval (code)</td><td>~94%</td><td>~90% (Code 4.5)</td></tr>
            <tr><td>GPQA (graduate reasoning)</td><td>~68%</td><td>~60% (3.5 Opus)</td></tr>
            <tr><td>MATH (competition)</td><td>~78%</td><td>~71% (3.5 Opus)</td></tr>
          </table>
          <p style="margin-top:0.5rem;font-size:0.88rem;color:var(--muted)">Benchmark figures are approximate and drawn from publicly reported evaluations. Always verify against vendor documentation for the most current numbers.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="section" aria-labelledby="guidance">
          <h2 id="guidance">Practical Guidance</h2>
          <ul class="clean">
            <li><strong>Prompt design:</strong> use structured system prompts, explicit output formats and chain-of-thought instructions for best results.</li>
            <li><strong>Cost management:</strong> Opus is the highest-cost tier. Use Sonnet or Haiku for simpler tasks and route complex queries to Opus.</li>
            <li><strong>Validation:</strong> always review generated code and factual claims before production use — no LLM is infallible.</li>
            <li><strong>Data privacy:</strong> review Anthropic's data-handling and retention policies before sending sensitive information.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

